  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed development would result in the loss of usable private amenity space serving the existing dwelling at No. 47 Peacock Avenue and would fail to provide an adequate quantity and quality of private outdoor amenity space for both the proposed dwelling and the retained dwelling. Furthermore, insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate that satisfactory levels of daylight would be achieved within the proposed dwelling, having regard to the excessive depth of the ground-floor accommodation and the location of the kitchen area remote from external openings. Taken together, the proposal would fail to provide a satisfactory standard of external and internal residential accommodation for existing and proposed dwelling at No. 47 Peacock Avenue, and is contrary to Local Plan Policies SC1 and SC5, London Plan Policies D3 and D6, and the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - By reason of its enlarged footprint, the excessive depth of the ground floor rear extensions and increased plot coverage, the proposal would represent an overdevelopment of the site, resulting in a cramped and overly intensive form of development that fails to achieve an appropriate balance between built form and open space, to the detriment of the spacious suburban character of the area and the established pattern of development within the area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies SC1, CC1 and CC2 of the Hounslow Local Plan and Policies D3 and D4 of the London Plan."
  ],
